PROBLEM:
If we implement all the functionalities of an application in a single class, than a facade is
created inside class. Also, this will violate SRP,OCP. So to solve this problem, we use a DP
called as Facade D.P.

SOLUTION:
Instead of creating all the functions inside a single class, create separate classes for all the
functionalities, such that it will follow SRP.
Also, if we need to add a new functionality we can create a separate class of it, which follows
OCP.
Now, once the functionalities are defined we can call the methods from class in ordered manner.

